#{[17592186265714 :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (2,2)}\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+3x{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}}{{x}^{2}-2xy+{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{{2}^{3}-3({2}^{2})(2)+3(2)({2}^{2})-{2}^{3}}{{2}^{2}-2(2)(2)+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-24+24-8}{4-8+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (2,2)}\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+3x{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}}{{x}^{2}-2xy+{y}^{2}} & =\\lim_{x\\to (2,2)}\\frac{(x-y)^{3}}{(x-y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (2,2)}\\frac{(x-y)(x-y)^{2}}{(x-y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (2,2)}\\frac{(x-y)\\cancel{(x-y)^{2}}}{\\cancel{(x-y)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (2,2)}(x-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (2,2)}(x-y) & =2-2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $0.$"] [17592186265715 :question/problem "Find $\\lim_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}-xy}.$"] [17592186265715 :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}-xy} & =\\frac{(-1)^{2}-(-1)^{2}}{(-1)^{2}-(-1)(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-1}{1-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}-xy} & =\\lim_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{(x+y)(x-y)}{x(x-y)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{(x+y)\\cancel{(x-y)}}{x\\cancel{(x-y)}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{x+y}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{x+y}{x} & =\\frac{-1+(-1)}{(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)}{(-1)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $2.$"] [17592186265716 :question/problem "$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}+x-y}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}}=\n$$"] [17592186265716 :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}+x-y}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{0}-\\sqrt{0}+0-0}{\\sqrt{0}-\\sqrt{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-0+0-0}{0-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}+x-y}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}} & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}+x-y)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y})(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y})(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})+(x-y)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{x-y} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{x-y+(x-y)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{x-y} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{(x-y)(1+\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{x-y} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\cancel{(x-y)}(1+\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{\\cancel{x-y}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}(1+\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}(1+\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}) & =1+\\sqrt{0}+\\sqrt{0} \\\\  & =1+0+0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $1.$"] [17592186265717 :question/problem "$\\lim_{x\\to (1,2,-1)}\\frac{x\\sqrt{y+z}-1}{{x}^{2}(y+z)-1}=$"] [17592186265717 :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,2,-1)}\\frac{x\\sqrt{y+z}-1}{{x}^{2}(y+z)-1} & =\\frac{1\\sqrt{2+(-1)}-1}{({1}^{2})(2+(-1))-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-1}{1-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,2,-1)}\\frac{x\\sqrt{y+z}-1}{{x}^{2}(y+z)-1} & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,2,-1)}\\frac{(x\\sqrt{y+z}-1)(x\\sqrt{y+z}+1)}{({x}^{2}(y+z)-1)(x\\sqrt{y+z}+1)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,2,-1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}(y+z)-1}{({x}^{2}(y+z)-1)(x\\sqrt{y+z}+1)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,2,-1)}\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}(y+z)-1}}{\\cancel{({x}^{2}(y+z)-1)}(x\\sqrt{y+z}+1)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,2,-1)}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{y+z}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,2,-1)}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{y+z}+1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\sqrt{2+(-1)}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{2}.$"] [17592186265718 :question/problem "Find $\\lim_{x\\to (1,0,1)}\\frac{x+y-{z}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x+y}-z}.$"] [17592186265718 :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,0,1)}\\frac{x+y-{z}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x+y}-z} & =\\frac{1+0-{1}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+0}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+0-1}{1-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,0,1)}\\frac{x+y-{z}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x+y}-z} & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,0,1)}\\frac{(x+y-{z}^{2})(\\sqrt{x+y}+z)}{(\\sqrt{x+y}-z)(\\sqrt{x+y}+z)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,0,1)}\\frac{(x+y-{z}^{2})(\\sqrt{x+y}+z)}{x+y-{z}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,0,1)}\\frac{\\cancel{(x+y-{z}^{2})}(\\sqrt{x+y}+z)}{\\cancel{x+y-{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,0,1)}(\\sqrt{x+y}+z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,0,1)}(\\sqrt{x+y}+z) & =\\sqrt{1+0}+1 \\\\  & =1+0+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $2.$"] [17592186265719 :question/problem "$\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}-3}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}=$"] [17592186265719 :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}-3}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{({0}^{2})({0}^{2})+9}-3}{({0}^{2})({0}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-3}{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}-3}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}} & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}-3)(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3)}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9-9}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+9}+3} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{({0}^{2})({0}^{2})+9}+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9}+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{6}.$"] [17592186283230 :answer/value "-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +C"] [17592186283335 :answer/value "sin⁡\\theta +C"] [17592186283440 :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +C"] [17592186283494 :answer/value "-sin⁡\\theta +C"] [17592186283552 :answer/value "-cos⁡\\theta +C"] [17592186284994 :answer/value "sec⁡\\theta +C"] [17592186285251 :answer/value "{e}^{x}sec⁡x+{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x"] [17592186285366 :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x+{e}^{x}tan⁡x"] [17592186285621 :answer/value "{e}^{x}{csc}^{2}⁡x+{e}^{x}tan⁡x"] [17592186285660 :answer/value "csc⁡xcot⁡x+C"] [17592186285849 :answer/value "\\frac{cos⁡x}{ln⁡10}-sin⁡xlog⁡x"] [17592186286129 :answer/value "{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x+tan⁡x"] [17592186286442 :answer/value "\\frac{cos⁡x}{x}-sin⁡xlog⁡x"] [17592186286464 :answer/value "\\frac{cos⁡x}{xln⁡10}+sin⁡xlog⁡x"]}
